@startuml context-map
!include _style.puml
title Playground context map (draft: the relationship words are for the owner to confirm)
' One idea: which bounded context asks which, and how. An arrow points from the side that ASKS to the side that ANSWERS.
' Sources: docs/domain/contexts/BC-ACCESS.md, BC-PROJECTS.md, BC-AUDIT.md (their refers_to and ports_needed), ADR 0002
' (Caller), ADR 0003 and 0011 (Audit as its own context), decision 14.
' NOT drawn: what is inside each context (access-design.puml, projects-design.puml, audit-design.puml), the actors
' (usecases-access.puml), the web server (bff-design.puml), the ports by name beyond the label on a line.
' Status: Access and Projects are built. Audit is built inside Access today and is being split out (decision 14, "planned"
' in BC-AUDIT). Files, Endpoints and Evaluations are named by BC-PROJECTS and have no page yet.
' Every line is dashed: no context imports another. Each goes through a port, and a bridge in composition/ (the one place
' that knows all three) answers it. The architecture tests enforce this.
' References between contexts are by identity only (an account id, a project id), never by a shared model.

skinparam rectangle {
  RoundCorner 8
}
skinparam rectangle<<generic>> {
  BackgroundColor #E8F0FE
  BorderColor #555555
}
skinparam rectangle<<supporting>> {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDE7
  BorderColor #555555
}
skinparam rectangle<<planned>> {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #888888
  BorderStyle dashed
}
skinparam cloud<<external>> {
  BackgroundColor #ECEFF1
  BorderColor #555555
}
top to bottom direction

package "Playground API: one folder for each bounded context" {
  rectangle "Projects\nbuilt" as PRJ <<supporting>>
  rectangle "Access\nbuilt" as ACC <<generic>>
  rectangle "Audit\nbeing split out of Access" as AUD <<generic>>
}

rectangle "Files, Endpoints, Evaluations\nno page yet" as PLN <<planned>>
cloud "Keycloak" as KC <<external>>

PRJ ..> ACC : Customer / Supplier\n(AccountStatus, People)
PRJ ..> AUD : Customer / Supplier\n(AuditLog)
ACC ..> AUD : Customer / Supplier\n(AuditLog)
ACC ..> KC : ACL\n(IdentityProvider)
PLN ..> PRJ : by project id only

note bottom of AUD
  Projects never imports Access. It receives a Caller
  (account id, is administrator), set once by the route
  guard (ADR 0002).
  Audit never changes an account, a role, a project or a
  member. It holds entries about them. Append only.
  The token's sub becomes our account id. Keycloak's
  words stay on its side of the ACL.
end note

legend bottom
|= Word |= Meaning |
| Customer / Supplier | The side that asks, and the side that answers and plans for it |
| ACL | We translate an outside system so its words stay out of ours |
| dashed arrow | goes through a port, answered by a bridge in composition/ |
endlegend
@enduml
